# P7a (R-7-1): the `@yanlinglabs` scope resolves to GitHub Packages, not public npm.
#
# The arc's publish target is GitHub Packages until the public `@yanlinglabs` npm org is verified and
# 2FA-hardened (the public-npm publish is P9's). This file makes that the DEFAULT for the scope, so a
# publish or an install cannot silently reach the wrong registry because someone forgot a flag —
# which is the failure mode that matters here: a private package published to public npm cannot be
# un-published.
#
# NO CREDENTIALS LIVE HERE. Reading a private package needs a token with `read:packages`, and
# publishing one needs `write:packages`; both arrive from the environment (CI's `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN`, a
# developer's own `~/.npmrc`), never from a file in the repository.
@yanlinglabs:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com

# P7a pre-publish (item 5; user ruling 2026-09-08: publish to BOTH registries). The scope line above
# stays the DEFAULT -- an install or a publish with no explicit registry still goes to GitHub
# Packages, which is the safe direction. The npm leg of `release.yml` overrides it for that one
# command with `--registry https://registry.npmjs.org`.
#
# This line is the AUTH for that override, and it is still credential-free: `${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}` is
# expanded by npm from the environment at run time (CI supplies `secrets.NPM_TOKEN`, a developer
# their own token), never read from this file. A literal token here would be committed, and the
# release pack's own scan refuses a credentials-shaped file in any tarball -- this file is not in any
# `files` list, but the rule is the same one.
//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
